    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded when Stephen I was crowned in 1000 or 1001, it brought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magyars">Magyars</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin-christendom">Latin Christendom</a>.</li><li>Royal counties, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> church and the union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> in 1102 made it a major power of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</li><li>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> devastated it in 1241; after rebuilding, baronial power grew until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arpad">Árpád</a> male line ended in 1301.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-bull-of-1222">Golden Bull of 1222</a>, issued seven years after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magna-carta">Magna Carta</a>, allowed the nobles to resist a king who broke its terms.</p></aside>
    </section>

